# Everything the site serves. The editor runs entirely client-side over
# localStorage, so there is no frame-embedding story to support and nothing
# downstream that needs a referrer. The CSP is not here: SvelteKit hashes its
# inline init script per page, so the policy rides each prerendered page as a
# <meta> tag (vite.config.ts `csp`) and 404.html carries its own — a header
# would need 'unsafe-inline' or per-build hashes. x-frame-options stays,
# because frame-ancestors is the one directive a <meta> policy cannot carry.
/*
  x-content-type-options: nosniff
  x-frame-options: DENY
  referrer-policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/_app/immutable/*
  cache-control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
